# Table of kinds of work for hooks/write_advice.py. One line is one rule, three fields:
#
#   <kind of work> | <target masks, comma-separated> | <skill>
#
# A mask is matched against the file NAME, not the path. A line starting with a hash is a comment.
# Adding a kind of work means adding a line: the hook is not edited.
#
# Why the table lives here and not in the engine's config.toml: that file is machine-local, sits in
# .gitignore and does not ship with the plugin — the table would never reach projects from there.

markup | *.html,*.htm,*.css,*.scss,*.sass,*.less,*.jinja,*.jinja2,*.j2,*.vue,*.svelte | retainer:frontend-taste
test | test_*.sh,test_*.py,*_test.py | retainer:test-generation
